From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_avfoundation: rebuild the output around a shared centre

Lucid Engine's AVFoundation audio output plays decoded PCM through
AVSampleBufferAudioRenderer, as upstream does, and passes AC-3 and E-AC-3
through AVPlayer, which upstream refuses. This patch rewrites
audio/out/ao_avfoundation.m as the output's shared centre; the next three
patches add the decoded PCM sink, the passthrough start-up supervision and
the compressed passthrough sink.

The output's decisions are plain C that reaches mpv, AVFoundation and the
audio session only through operation tables, so the shipped code can be
driven by test fakes on the build host; the Objective-C files make the
Apple framework calls. This patch adds:

- ao_avfoundation_core.h and .c: trace edges and the detail window that
  follows each one, the prefetch guard both sinks use, the process-wide
  passthrough block, the audio session steps, and the order in which init
  refuses formats, sets up the session, creates the queue and opens a sink;
- ao_avfoundation_av.h: the state the Objective-C files share;
- ao_avfoundation.m: driver registration with the ao-avfoundation-*
  options (max-lookahead exists on tvOS only), the output's serial queue,
  tagged so that work already on it runs inline, the AVAudioSession calls
  behind TARGET_OS_IPHONE, and the routing of every driver call to the sink
  init opened.

Audio session: with manage-audio-session on (the default), init sets the
category (playback) and mode (movie playback) and activates the session,
and uninit and a failed init deactivate it, notifying other apps. With it
off, the output never sets the category or mode, activates or
deactivates. Either way it declares multichannel content for spdif formats
and for more than two channels (iOS and tvOS 15 and later), and sets the
preferred output channel count for PCM. A PCM init clears the passthrough
block first, and an spdif format with accept-compressed off is refused
before any session call.

The macOS device list and device selection stay as patch 0002 left them,
and "please use coreaudio_exclusive instead" is still logged only where
the CoreAudio output exists. meson.build lists every file of the output.
Applies to mpv v0.41.0 with patch 0002.

